    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Neovascular age-related macular degeneration, left eye, responding (H35.3221)</content>. Gain of 9 letters (55 to 64) and central subfield thickness down from 418 to 322 µm, with residual fluid. Second loading injection given today without complication. [S]<list><item>Third loading injection in four weeks.</item><item>Same-day call for warning signs.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Intermediate dry age-related macular degeneration, right eye (H35.3112)</content>. Stable on dilated examination; no new distortion. [S]<list><item>Continue the AREDS2 supplement and daily Amsler checks.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Best-corrected visual acuity (ETDRS letters)</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Left 64 letters, up 9 from baseline. The right eye is followed by Amsler grid and dilated examination during loading</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Optical coherence tomography of the macula</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Left eye: central subfield thickness 322 µm with residual fluid</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Intraocular pressure before and after injection</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Before injection 15 mmHg left; after injection, optic nerve perfused and counting fingers</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Fluorescein angiography or OCT angiography</td><td>If the response is poor or the picture atypical</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Responding as expected to loading, which supports the diagnosis</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Dilated examination of the fellow (right) eye</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Large drusen unchanged; no fluid</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Intravitreal injection safety</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Small subconjunctival hemorrhage after the first injection, resolved; no inflammation. Second loading dose today</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Teaching on warning signs of endophthalmitis and retinal detachment</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Reviewed again</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Daily home Amsler grid, each eye</td><td>Daily</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Daily checks recorded; no change in the right eye</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>AREDS2 supplement for intermediate AMD</td><td>Daily, long term</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taking it daily</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Low-vision rehabilitation, with home fall-risk review and a driving assessment</td><td>Once central vision is reduced; review as vision changes</td><td>Referred</td><td>Evaluation booked for next month</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-2)</td><td>At follow-up, because vision loss raises the risk of depression; periodically at 65 or older</td><td>Due</td><td>Planned at the July primary care review</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Gain at least 10 ETDRS letters in the left eye by the end of the loading phase. In progress; target 1968-05-07 [S]</item><item>Dry macula on OCT (central subfield thickness below 300 um, no fluid) by the end of the loading phase. In progress; target 1968-05-07 [S]</item><item>Check the Amsler grid daily for each eye and report any change the same day. In progress; target 1968-07-02 [S]</item><item>Complete a low-vision rehabilitation evaluation and set up studio lighting and magnification by the July visit. In progress; target 1968-07-02 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Age-Related Macular Degeneration Preferred Practice Pattern (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, cataract and glaucoma monographs (eye-examination items) (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Retina visit in four weeks for the third loading injection. Next scheduled visit 1968-05-07: eight-week retina follow-up with OCT and third injection. [S]</paragraph></text>

